<title>BRAZIL: Brazil coffee co-ops report milder evening temps.</title>
<headline>Brazil coffee co-ops report milder evening temps.</headline>
<dateline>RIO DE JANEIRO 1997-06-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>Brazilian coffee co-operatives and weather centres in key growing regions reported milder temperatures late Monday evening than had been seen on Sunday night.</p>
<p>A polar air mass passing through the region led to frosts early Monday in lower-lying regions where coffee is not grown. No damage was reported to the coffee crop.</p>
<p>Coffee grown on higher slopes normally sees warmer temperatures than those registered in dips in many key areas.</p>
<p>Temperatures in degrees Celsius as reported by cooperatives and weather monitoring centers were as follows by 2330 local/ 0230 GMT with comparisons for June 8.</p>
<p>							  June 9    June 8</p>
<p> PARANA, Londrina				     13	  8</p>
<p> SAO PAULO, Presidente Prudente		   13	  9</p>
<p> SAO PAULO, Franca				    11	  6</p>
<p> MINAS GERAIS, Sao Sebastiao do Paraiso	9.5	  7</p>
<p> MINAS GERAIS, Pocos de Caldas		     6	 4.5</p>
<p>((-Caroline Bulloch, Rio de Janeiro newsroom, 5521 5074151))</p>
</text>
